# Baste

## Register

product

## Users

Designers and developers building interfaces for people with specific cultural influences. The Studio is a workroom for editing personas, fitting design tokens, collecting references and generating assets; the public site explains the method.

## Product Purpose

Turn films, music, spaces, tools and obsessions into usable, culturally specific UI assets. Explore diverse candidates and retain a useful archive, rather than collapsing the process into a single answer.

## Brand Personality

Tactile, attentive, particular. The existing house style is a tailor's atelier: pattern paper, ink, thread and chalk. Keep its quiet framing so a persona's own palette remains legible.

## Anti-references

Generic demographic personas, interchangeable AI asset galleries, decorative controls that obscure the fitting process, and account or payment states that imply access before it is verified.

## Design Principles

- Cultural influences are the measurements; demographics alone do not determine a fitting.
- Preserve diverse options and show useful production states.
- Reuse the established atelier components and tokens.
- Keep local work, provider credentials and hosted account state understandable.
- Show verified availability, failures and next actions in the flow where they matter.

## Accessibility & Inclusion

Preserve the existing semantic forms, keyboard focus, skip links, readable text contrast and reduced-motion alternatives. Keep controls usable on narrow screens with accessible names when labels collapse.

This context records the existing AGENT_REFERENCE.md, Panda tokens and Studio component conventions; it does not introduce a new visual direction.
import { component$, useContextProvider, useStore, useVisibleTask$ } from "@builder.io/qwik";
import type { DocumentHead } from "@builder.io/qwik-city";
import { css } from "styled-system/css";
import {
  API_KEY,
  StudioCtx,
  connectStudio,
  initialState,
  toast,
  type PersonaTab,
  type StudioView,
} from "~/components/studio/context";
import { Topbar } from "~/components/studio/topbar";
import { Rail } from "~/components/studio/rail";
import { Toasts } from "~/components/studio/toasts";
import { Workspace } from "~/components/studio/workspace";
import { PersonaForm } from "~/components/studio/flows/persona-form";
import { DecomposeFlow } from "~/components/studio/flows/decompose";
import { RemixFlow } from "~/components/studio/flows/remix";
import { SettingsFlow } from "~/components/studio/flows/settings";
import { DEFAULT_API } from "~/lib/api";

const TABS: PersonaTab[] = ["fitting", "tokens", "generate", "moodboard", "brandkit", "feedback", "editor"];
const FLOWS: StudioView[] = ["decompose", "remix", "settings", "tailor"];

export default component$(() => {
  const state = useStore(initialState(), { deep: true });
  useContextProvider(StudioCtx, state);

  // eslint-disable-next-line qwik/no-use-visible-task
  useVisibleTask$(async () => {
    const q = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);
    const tab = q.get("tab") as PersonaTab | null;
    const flow = q.get("flow") as StudioView | null;
    if (q.get("persona")) state.selectedId = q.get("persona")!;
    if (tab && TABS.includes(tab)) state.tab = tab;
    if (q.get("new")) state.view = "new";
    else if (flow && FLOWS.includes(flow)) state.view = flow;

    let base = DEFAULT_API;
    try {
      base = localStorage.getItem(API_KEY) || DEFAULT_API;
    } catch {
      /* storage unavailable — use the default */
    }
    await connectStudio(state, base);
